WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:03.302
-Many of
President Trump's nominees

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:05.004
to top government positions
have been questionable,

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:07.707
but perhaps none more so than
his choice to head

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:09.275
the Department of Energy,
Rick Perry,

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:12.745
who once wanted to abolish the
very agency he's now leading.

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:14.213
So we decided to take a break

00:00:14.213 --> 00:00:16.415
from the breaking news of
the day and see how he's doing.

00:00:16.415 --> 00:00:18.751
It's time for "The Check In."

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:20.219 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:22.655
[ Bell dings ]

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:25.191
Now most people were probably
surprised that Donald Trump

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:27.326
nominated former
Governor of Texas, Rick Perry,

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:28.527
to lead
the Department of Energy,

00:00:28.527 --> 00:00:30.896
as he was once Trump's rival
in trying to get

00:00:30.896 --> 00:00:33.833
the Republican nomination
for President for 2016.

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:35.935
In fact, Perry even called
Trump's candidacy

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:38.037
a cancer on conservativism.

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:41.841
And Trump countered with some
of his trademark insult comedy.

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:45.245
-I see Rick Perry the other day,
and he's so --

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:47.246
You know, he's doing very poorly
in the polls.

00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:50.316
He put glasses on so people
will think he is smart.

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:52.384
[ Laughter ]
And it just doesn't work!

00:00:52.384 --> 00:00:55.788
You know, people can see
through the glasses.

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:58.124
But he's got the glasses,
the whole deal.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:59.759
"Oh-oh, oh, Trump, huh."

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.794
-The list of reasons to dislike
Trump is long, I know,

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:04.363
but I'm gonna add the laziness
of his impressions.

00:01:04.363 --> 00:01:06.832
"Oh, oh-ho-ho-uh..."

00:01:06.832 --> 00:01:08.868
[ Laughter ]
That could be anybody.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:12.671
[ Imitating Trump ] Meanwhile,
you got Marco Rubio. Oh...uh...

00:01:12.671 --> 00:01:15.441
[ Laughter ]
Then Ted Cruz is like oh...uh...

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:16.876
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:18.311
[ Normal voice ] Now the great
irony in Perry's nomination

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:21.047
perhaps lost only on Trump
is that the Department of Energy

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:24.050
is one of the agencies Perry
said he wanted to abolish

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.753
back in 2011 when
he was running for President.

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:29.522
That is, before he forgot it was
the agency he wanted

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:30.923
to get rid of.

00:01:30.923 --> 00:01:33.058
-It's three agencies of
government when I get there that

00:01:33.058 --> 00:01:37.663
are gone -- commerce, education
and the, uh...

00:01:37.663 --> 00:01:39.699
what's the third one there?
Let's see.

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:41.367
-You can't name the third one?

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:44.636
-The third agency of government
I would do away with,

00:01:44.636 --> 00:01:47.807
education, uh, the, uh...

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:49.141
[ Laughter ]
-Commerce.

00:01:49.141 --> 00:01:52.712
-I...commerce, and let's see.
-Oh, my.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:55.114
-I can't.
The third one, I can't. Sorry.

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:56.582
[ Laughter ]
Oops.

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:59.586
-Now, that should have
been it.

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:01.020
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:04.224
That should have been the last
time anyone saw Rick Perry.

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:06.525
Once you Bill Buckner
a debate like that,

00:02:06.525 --> 00:02:09.995
you should be the answer
to a trivia question, at best.

00:02:09.995 --> 00:02:12.765
The only thing worse would be if
you straight up didn't know

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:15.735
the voting age
or when election day was.

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:19.072
-Those of you that are -- will
be 21 by November the 12th,

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:21.507
I ask for your support
and your vote.

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:23.642
-[ Groans ]
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.642 --> 00:02:26.979
No, it's 18 to vote, and
Election Day was November 6th.

00:02:26.979 --> 00:02:28.847
So we didn't know the agency
you wanted to abolish

00:02:28.847 --> 00:02:30.849
or when election day was
or what the voting age is,

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:33.753
but surely -- surely Rick Perry
knows where he is

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.454
at any given time.

00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:39.559
-There are many other states
that embrace those conservative,

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:44.296
uh, values -- the approach that
we've taken over the years.

00:02:44.296 --> 00:02:48.601
I'm in one today in Florida.
You look at South Carolina.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.637
You look at Florida.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.874
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:57.543
-Okay. But that, guys...

00:02:57.543 --> 00:03:01.113
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:03.416
I know it seems like we're
piling on, but that has to be

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:04.983
the most embarrassing clip
of Rick Perry. What's that?

00:03:04.983 --> 00:03:07.586
There are more? How many more?
Thousands more.

00:03:07.586 --> 00:03:09.087
All right, well,
let's just go with one more

00:03:09.087 --> 00:03:10.490
for the sake of time.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.458
-Rick Perry!

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:14.693 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:14.693 --> 00:03:16.596
-♪ Ice, ice baby ♪

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:20.499 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:20.499 --> 00:03:23.736
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:26.906
-That's the guy currently in
charge of our nuclear arsenal.

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:29.641
No, not Vanilla Ice.

00:03:29.641 --> 00:03:32.011
Vanilla Ice would be a step up.

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.479
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:34.680
Now you would think that
Rick Perry would take the time

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.449
to familiarize himself
with the kind of work

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:40.252
the Department of Energy, whose
budget exceeds $30 billion does.

00:03:40.252 --> 00:03:41.587
But according to
the "New York Times,"

00:03:41.587 --> 00:03:44.290
when then-President-elect Trump
offered Perry the job...

00:04:03.075 --> 00:04:05.344
Imagine finding out after you
accepted a job that

00:04:05.344 --> 00:04:09.315
the job description included
managing nuclear weapons.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:12.652
I got pissed when I found out
mine included animal segments.

00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:17.590
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:20.259
So Perry accepted a role he was
confused about, and then somehow

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:21.894
made it through
the confirmation process.

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:23.929
Although we shouldn't be
surprised, as the Senate also

00:04:23.929 --> 00:04:26.332
confirmed Betsy DeVos
for Secretary of Education,

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:28.000
already resigned Tom Price

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.002
for Secretary
of Health and Human Services,

00:04:30.002 --> 00:04:33.406
and a haunted doll
as Secretary of Commerce.

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:35.674
But we would hope that once he
officially had the job,

00:04:35.674 --> 00:04:36.909
Perry would try to learn more

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:38.477
from someone like
his predecessor,

00:04:38.477 --> 00:04:41.581
Dr. Ernest Moniz,
a nuclear physicist.

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:43.983
Interesting fact -- Moniz became
a nuclear physicist

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.284
when his high school
guidance counselor

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:47.319
took a look at him
and said it's either that

00:04:47.319 --> 00:04:49.322
or Ben Franklin impersonator.

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:51.090
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.925
But according to a source cited
in a "Vanity Fair" report

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:55.794
from July, Perry barely spent
any time with Moniz.

00:04:55.794 --> 00:04:58.598
According to the reporter's
sources, he writes that Perry...

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:10.610
But in Perry's defense,
he doesn't doesn't really need

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.045
to be an expert
in nuclear energy when his boss

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:14.747
already has such a good handle
on it.

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:17.282
-You know what uranium is,
right? Think of nuclear weapons

00:05:17.282 --> 00:05:21.220
and other things, like lots
of things are done with uranium,

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.089
including some bad things.

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:24.757
-Perry saw that and thought,

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:27.126
"Oh, he's already up
to speed. We're good."

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:29.261
But reports started surfacing
back in the summer

00:05:29.261 --> 00:05:31.763
that Perry had
fallen out of favor with Trump

00:05:31.763 --> 00:05:33.532
and that Trump was actually
looking to replace him,

00:05:33.532 --> 00:05:35.701
which is also when
this happened.

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:37.570
<i> -Russia's messing
 with U.S. politicians again,</i>

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:39.638
<i> but this time,
 it's Russian pranksters,</i>

00:05:39.638 --> 00:05:42.541
<i> and they tricked Secretary
 of Energy, Rick Perry,</i>

00:05:42.541 --> 00:05:44.610
<i> into believing he was having
 a conversation</i>

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.779
<i> with the Ukrainian
 Prime Minister.</i>

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:48.514
-That's right.
Russian pranksters pretending

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:50.483
to be the Prime Minster
of Ukraine...

00:05:52.752 --> 00:05:56.389
...with Perry.
A 20-minute prank call.

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:58.424
Even the Jerky Boys would say,
"hey, man, this is fun,

00:05:58.424 --> 00:06:01.560
but we have places to be."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:04.162
And we don't know for sure how
Perry recovered from that

00:06:04.162 --> 00:06:06.532
and won Trump back over, but it
may have something to do

00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:09.201
with Perry's new controversial
energy proposal

00:06:09.201 --> 00:06:11.871
which would basically force
consumers to subsidize old,

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:14.206
failing coal and nuclear
power plants

00:06:14.206 --> 00:06:15.975
that would otherwise likely
be obsolete.

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:18.478
According to reports
and analysis, this plan would...

00:06:24.951 --> 00:06:27.587
So why provide this preferential
treatment to aging industries

00:06:27.587 --> 00:06:29.722
at the potential expense
of millions of consumers?

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:32.258
Well, according to reports,
Perry's plan...

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:42.968
Ah, yes, Bob Murray,
the litigious coal tycoon,

00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:45.771
who apparently needs this
administration's help so much,

00:06:45.771 --> 00:06:48.374
reports say that his company,
Murray Energy...

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:54.780
Ugh. Imagine if
your whole livelihood

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:56.949
came down to Rick Perry.

00:06:56.949 --> 00:07:00.319
It's like when the Vietnam War
came down to Forrest Gump.

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:02.154
[ Laughter ]
But it's not just Perry.

00:07:02.154 --> 00:07:03.622
And of course, as with other
government agencies,

00:07:03.622 --> 00:07:06.124
Trump has made other
questionable hires

00:07:06.124 --> 00:07:07.827
at the Department of Energy,
like bringing in

00:07:07.827 --> 00:07:11.430
Eric Trump's brother-in-law,
Kyle Yunaska, for example.

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:14.066
Yunaska, who's the brother of
Eric Trump's wife, Lara Trump,

00:07:14.066 --> 00:07:15.801
was recently
promoted to the position

00:07:15.801 --> 00:07:18.203
of Chief of Staff for
the department's office

00:07:18.203 --> 00:07:20.739
of Energy Policy
and Systems Analysis.

00:07:20.739 --> 00:07:23.041
Sounds like a pretty important
job for someone who must have

00:07:23.041 --> 00:07:24.844
an impressive background
in energy policy.

00:07:24.844 --> 00:07:28.014
Well, according to "Newsweek,"
Yunaska's...

00:07:35.121 --> 00:07:36.922
Okay, fine, but is there
anything else on his résumé

00:07:36.922 --> 00:07:39.124
that shows he's qualified?
Let's see. Oh! There.

00:07:39.124 --> 00:07:40.393
Reports say...

00:07:46.698 --> 00:07:48.367
And there's a picture.

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:51.369
That's him on the end.
-Oh!

00:07:51.369 --> 00:07:52.938
-Now for someone who works for
the Department of Energy,

00:07:52.938 --> 00:07:56.175
it's not exactly reassuring that
he doesn't even have the energy

00:07:56.175 --> 00:07:59.078
to get off the ground.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:59.078 --> 00:08:01.714
So we have inexperienced leaders
seemingly beholden,

00:08:01.714 --> 00:08:03.515
special interests,
and family members

00:08:03.515 --> 00:08:05.084
getting top jobs
at the Department of Energy,

00:08:05.084 --> 00:08:08.454
So at this point, if something
goes wrong, the only explanation

00:08:08.454 --> 00:08:11.090
I guess we should expect is, uh,
what's the elegant phrase

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:12.324
I'm looking for?

00:08:12.324 --> 00:08:13.959
-Oops.
-That's what I thought.

00:08:13.959 --> 00:08:16.228
This has been "The Check In."

00:08:16.228 --> 00:08:17.696 line:0%
♪♪

00:08:17.696 --> 00:08:19.031
[ Bell dings ]

